<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Monroe called the clinic and was seen the same day. Since yesterday morning she has had burning when she passes urine, needs to go every half hour, feels she has not emptied her bladder, and has a dull ache low in the middle of her pelvis. It began two days after intercourse. She has had no fever, chills, back or side pain, nausea, blood in the urine, or vaginal discharge or itching. This pain is different from her usual endometriosis pain: it is low and central, it is tied to passing urine, and it came on suddenly. She has taken the continuous pill every day without a bleed and has not needed naproxen this week. She had one bladder infection years ago. Her mood has been steadier since she started therapy, and she has had no thoughts of suicide or self-harm. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Yesterday morning, two days after intercourse</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Low central pelvis; burning in the urethra</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>About 30 hours</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Burning on urination, frequency, urgency, incomplete emptying</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Discomfort 4 of 10; sleep broken by getting up to pass urine</td></tr><tr><td>Timing</td><td>Constant, worse on passing urine</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Continuous combined pill for five weeks; no bleeding; one bladder infection years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Drinking more water; no medicine taken</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>No fever, back or side pain, blood in the urine, vaginal discharge, or thoughts of suicide or self-harm</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

