  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute uncomplicated cystitis (N30.00)</content>. Typical acute uncomplicated cystitis: sudden burning, frequency and urgency after intercourse, with leukocyte esterase and nitrite on the dipstick and no fever, flank pain or tenderness to suggest kidney infection. Urine pregnancy test negative. A urine culture was sent because she has a chronic pelvic pain condition and a clear result will help if symptoms recur. Nitrofurantoin does not reduce the effect of her contraceptive pill. [S]<list><item>Nitrofurantoin 100 mg twice daily with food for 5 days.</item><item>Fluids; passing urine after intercourse.</item><item>Return or call for fever, back or side pain, vomiting, blood in the urine, or no improvement in 48 hours.</item><item>Culture result by phone.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Endometriosis with a left ovarian endometrioma (N80.102)</content>. No bleeding and no endometriosis pain flare on the continuous pill. Today&apos;s pain is from the bladder infection, not a flare; bladder endometriosis is unlikely because the symptoms are sudden and not tied to her cycle and there is no blood in the urine. [S]<list><item>Continue the continuous combined pill daily.</item><item>Naproxen only if needed, with food.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Major depressive disorder, single episode, moderate (F32.1)</content>. Mood steadier after four therapy sessions. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide or self-harm; the safety plan and the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline are in her phone. The PHQ-9 was not repeated today because the visit was for the infection. [S]<list><item>Continue therapy every two weeks.</item><item>PHQ-9 at the preventive visit next month.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: ESHRE guideline: endometriosis (2022); U.S. Selected Practice Recommendations for Contraceptive Use, 2024 (2024); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); International clinical practice guidelines for the treatment of acute uncomplicated cystitis and pyelonephritis in women: a 2010 update by the Infectious Diseases Society of America and the European Society for Microbiology and Infectious Diseases (2010)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Culture result by phone. Preventive visit next month as booked, or sooner as above. Next scheduled visit 1956-08-17: periodic adult preventive visit with pregnancy planning. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
